ParserTest
├── parseNumber
│   ├── given a bare number
│   │   ├── it parses an integer
│   │   ├── it parses a decimal
│   │   └── it parses zero
│   ├── given grouping separators
│   │   ├── given US grouping
│   │   │   ├── it reads a comma as thousands
│   │   │   └── it reads a dot as the decimal point
│   │   ├── given EU grouping
│   │   │   ├── it reads a dot as thousands
│   │   │   └── it reads a comma as the decimal point
│   │   ├── given Indian lakh grouping
│   │   │   └── it reads the two-digit groups
│   │   └── given Swiss apostrophe grouping
│   │       ├── it reads a straight apostrophe
│   │       └── it reads a typographic apostrophe
│   ├── given exactly three digits after a single dot
│   │   ├── given the caller expects US decimals
│   │   │   └── it reads them as a decimal
│   │   └── given the caller does not
│   │       └── it reads them as thousands
│   ├── given a magnitude suffix
│   │   ├── it reads it case-insensitively
│   │   └── it applies the right magnitude for each letter
│   ├── given a spelled-out multiplier
│   │   ├── it matches the whole word rather than a prefix
│   │   ├── it handles compound multipliers
│   │   └── it handles non-English words
│   └── given input that is not a number
│       ├── it returns null for letters
│       └── it returns null for an empty string
├── isBetterMatch
│   ├── given the candidate starts earlier
│   │   └── it wins
│   ├── given the candidate starts later
│   │   └── it loses
│   └── given both start at the same offset
│       ├── given the candidate is longer
│       │   └── it wins
│       └── given the candidate is no longer
│           └── it loses
└── parsePrice
    ├── given a symbol before the amount
    │   ├── it reads a dollar sign
    │   ├── it reads a euro sign
    │   └── it reads a pound sign
    ├── given the page declares a language
    │   ├── given the language uses a comma decimal
    │   │   └── it reads the number that way
    │   └── given the language tag is not one the browser knows
    │       └── it falls back to a dot decimal rather than failing
    ├── given a code after the amount
    │   └── it reads the code
    ├── given several prices in one string
    │   └── it returns each of them
    ├── given a magnitude in the price
    │   ├── it reads a suffix letter
    │   └── it reads a spelled-out word
    ├── given a negative amount
    │   ├── it skips the negative price
    │   └── it still reads both ends of a range
    ├── given an ambiguous symbol
    │   ├── given the page states its own currency
    │   │   ├── it beats the guess from the hostname
    │   │   └── given the page names a currency the symbol cannot mean
    │   │       └── it ignores the page and keeps the guess
    │   ├── given the hostname names a country
    │   │   └── it resolves to that country's currency
    │   ├── given that currency is not enabled
    │   │   └── it falls back to an enabled candidate
    │   ├── given the page language disambiguates
    │   │   └── it resolves from the language
    │   └── given nothing disambiguates
    │       └── it resolves to the default reading
    ├── given a dollar sign claimed by a prefix
    │   ├── given the prefix names a supported currency
    │   │   └── it reads that currency
    │   └── given the prefix names an unsupported one
    │       └── it reads nothing rather than guessing US dollars
    ├── given a hostname-restricted pattern
    │   ├── it applies on that site
    │   ├── it does not apply elsewhere
    │   └── it reads a site's split euro-and-cent markup
    ├── given the same price appears twice in one string
    │   ├── it returns both of them
    │   └── it keeps them at their own positions
    ├── given two readings overlap in position
    │   ├── it keeps the longer match
    │   ├── it keeps the one that starts earlier
    │   ├── it discards the shorter one
    │   └── it keeps the reading whose symbol is actually in the text
    ├── given a currency is not enabled
    │   └── it returns nothing for that currency
    └── given text with no price in it
        └── it returns nothing
